"open_issues":1818,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\nDespite what the [documentation](https://docs.bazel.build/versions/master/build-ref.html#workspace) says, the presence of a WORKSPACE file in a subdirectory does not prevent that subdirectory from being visible to Bazel.\r\n\r\nEDIT: However, if the subdirectory with a WORKSPACE file is referred to as a local_repository in the main WORKSPACE, Bazel will then not traverse into it.\r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ touch WORKSPACE\r\n$ mkdir nested\r\n$ touch nested/WORKSPACE\r\n$ echo 'filegroup(name=\"hello\")' > nested/BUILD\r\n$ bazel build //nested:hello\r\n# succeeds\r\n\r\n# EDIT\r\n$ echo 'local_repository(name=\"nested\",path=\"nested\")' > WORKSPACE\r\n$ bazel build //nested:hello\r\n# fails\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\n\r\nDebian testing (gLinux), repros on latest macOS\r\n\r\n### What's the output of `bazel info release`?\r\n\r\nrelease 3.6.0\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12298/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12298/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]